  "implementation": "After endpoint chaining, project short bed strokes onto nearby continuous receiver paths. Replace a local receiver interval by a bounded detour through the unchanged short stroke. Both round connector beads must fit the valid support islands, final-brim keepout and other-role keepouts. Preserve role, height, flow ratio, non-reversible direction and receiver closure. Reject a detour that loses a printable-width region of the old footing. Stable candidate order makes exports deterministic. Scope remains per-instance first-layer derived support; original support collections, higher geometry and contact planning remain unchanged.",
  "limitations": "Parallel pattern spacing and truly disconnected regions are not replaced with arbitrary cross-region links. Software geometry/export tests do not measure deposited plastic. No install, commit or push."
